  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solidaridad - National Initiatives for Sustainable &amp; Climate-smart Oil-Palm Smallholders (NI-SCOPS) Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a second, five-year phase of the National Initiatives for Sustainable &amp; Climate-smart Oil-Palm Smallholders (NI-SCOPS) programme, a flagship oil-palm production programme that is currently operating in partnership with the governments of Indonesia, Malaysia, Ghana, Nigeria and the Netherlands. The aim of NI-SCOPS is to ensure landscapes where oil palms are grown and managed sustainably, and smallholders measurably benefit from their inclusion in palm oil markets. 

NI-SCOPS Phase II proposes extending the programme&#x2019;s implementation to Colombia and adding a focus on influential market countries and regions, namely India and Asia, the United Kingdom (UK) and the European Union (EU), particularly in the context of the impact of the forthcoming EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR 2023 1115) and UK due diligence legislation on forest risk commodities.

This project is being jointly funded by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs (BZ).</narrative>
  </description>
